# 10. News.js

`News.js` is responsible for getting the news from the API.

It can maintain the news articles inside its state.

Example:

```jsx
import React, { Component } from "react";
import NewsItem from "./NewsItem";

export default class News extends Component {

  constructor() {
    super();

    this.state = {
      articles: [],
      loading: false
    };
  }

  render() {
    return (
      <div>
        <h1>Top Headlines</h1>

        {this.state.articles.map((article) => {

          return (
            <NewsItem
              title={article.title}
              description={article.description}
              imageUrl={article.urlToImage}
              newsUrl={article.url}
            />
          );

        })}
      </div>
    );
  }
}
```

---

# 11. NewsItem.js

`NewsItem.js` displays one individual news article.

Example:

```jsx
import React, { Component } from "react";

export default class NewsItem extends Component {

  render() {

    return (
      <div>

        <img
          src={this.props.imageUrl}
          alt="news"
        />

        <h3>
          {this.props.title}
        </h3>

        <p>
          {this.props.description}
        </p>

        <a href={this.props.newsUrl}>
          Read More
        </a>

      </div>
    );
  }
}
```

Here we are receiving information through props.

