# 14. Using Props with API Data

The real power comes when we get data from an API.

For example, the API may return:

```json
{
  "title": "New technology launched",
  "description": "A new technology has been launched.",
  "urlToImage": "image.jpg",
  "url": "https://example.com"
}
```

We can pass this information to `NewsItem`:

```jsx
<NewsItem
  title={article.title}
  description={article.description}
  imageUrl={article.urlToImage}
  newsUrl={article.url}
/>
```

Notice that we are using:

```jsx
{article.title}
```

instead of writing the title manually.

---

# 15. Mapping News Articles

If the API gives us many articles:

```text
Article 1
Article 2
Article 3
Article 4
Article 5
```

We can use `.map()`.

Example:

```jsx
this.state.articles.map((article) => {

  return (
    <NewsItem
      title={article.title}
      description={article.description}
    />
  );

})
```

`.map()` goes through every article and creates a `NewsItem`.

So:

```text
5 articles
   ↓
.map()
   ↓
5 NewsItem components
```

